

***#MediVault-Lost in Transit: Fragmented Medical Records and Repeated Care Across Providers***



&#x09;MediVault is a patient-focused medical-record management prototype that helps users bring their prescriptions, laboratory reports, scanned documents, and other medical files together in one place. It organizes available information into a chronological timeline, extracts text from supported documents, generates AI-assisted summaries, and provides controlled sharing for selected records.



**##Problem Statement:**

&#x09;Patients with long-term conditions such as diabetes, hypertension, thyroid disorders, and asthma may visit multiple doctors, clinics, diagnostic laboratories, and pharmacies over time. Their medical history can become scattered across paper prescriptions, PDF reports, scanned documents, photographs, and files shared through messaging applications.

When patients change doctors, move to another city, or visit an emergency room, previous records may not be available when needed. Patients may struggle to remember earlier diagnoses, allergies, medicines, and dosages. Clinicians may therefore have to make decisions with incomplete information. This can contribute to repeated diagnostic tests, conflicting treatment information, delays, and gaps in continuity of care.

Manual sharing can also expose sensitive health information. Patients need a convenient way to organize their medical history, understand it, share selected records with the intended recipient, and stop access when it is no longer needed. 



**##Proposed Solution:**



MediVault helps patients bring their medical documents together and share selected records through a controlled access workflow. Its intended capabilities include:

* **Medical timeline:** organizes uploaded records by documented event date so users can review the sequence of reports and medical events.
* **OCR text extraction:** extracts readable text from supported scans and images, reducing the need to manually type document content.
* **AI report summarization:** produces a shorter, easier-to-read overview of medical-record entries, with references to source records.
* **Report management:** stores document metadata and links structured records to their original documents.
* **Guest Access:** enables a patient to share a selected set of records with a recipient without requiring that recipient to create a patient account.
* **Expiry and revocation:** limits sharing to a specified time window and allows the patient to end access.

MediVault supports record organization and sharing. It does not replace professional medical advice, diagnose conditions, or independently determine treatment.



